Request: PUT http://localhost:8000/api/settings/github-pat
Trigger: Save clicked with a >512-char value in the GitHub PAT field
(synthetic test values only, e.g. "ghp_" + "A"*5000 and "github_pat_" + "Z"*600
 — never a real credential).

Response: 422 Unprocessable Entity
Body shape (value truncated here to first 60 / last 20 chars — the LIVE
response from the server contains the FULL submitted string, not truncated):

{"detail":[{"type":"string_too_long","loc":["body","pat"],
 "msg":"String should have at most 512 characters",
 "input":"github_pat_ZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZ...[551 more chars]...ZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZ",
 "ctx":{"max_length":512}}]}

Confirmed via direct read of response-body (browser_network_request) that the
"input" field is NOT truncated by the server — it is the complete, exact
string the client submitted, byte for byte. Reproduced twice with two
different synthetic payloads (5004 chars and 611 chars), same shape both
times.

Frontend also fails to parse this error shape: instead of a friendly message
(as it correctly does for the 400 "GitHub rejected the PAT" case), it renders
the ENTIRE raw JSON string — including the embedded "input" field carrying
the submitted value — directly as visible page text under the PAT input.
